# MT1 (stream S15-threads) - the world render's cull waits for this frame's cell update (docs/PERF.md 6.10, 6.11).
# Exempt from the MSVC byte check; behind FNVNX_MT1_ON. A race the PC code has: main runs the whole world render
# (0x0086ff70 -> 0x008706b0 -> MainView 0x00873200, the cull) between starting the AI linear threads (0x86ec87) and
# joining them (0x008c7990), with no wait on the normal path, while AI linear thread 2 runs TES::FUN_00453550 (the
# Havok step and the cell's UpdateDownwardPass: the world transforms and bounds the cull reads). Under x86's TSO the
# torn reads were rare and short; on the A57 a 13-float NiTransform read during its write is a real outcome.

@@ MT1 src/fallout/misc/main.cpp 0x008706b0
# The render entry of the frame (called from 0x0086ff70, main.cpp ~13732): wait for thread 2's event 6 (set right
# after its FUN_00453550, ailineartaskthreadmanager.cpp:806; reset by FUN_008c78c0 when main starts the AI threads)
# before the shadow-scene node and the cull run. fnvnx_mt1_wait_cell_update(): toolchain/game/boot.cpp (no wait with
# one AI thread, bounded otherwise).
<<<
    bool f = NiAdditionalGeometryData::GetShadowSceneNodeForIndex(0)->FUN_00870770();
=== guarded
    if (FNVNX_MT1_ON)
        fnvnx_mt1_wait_cell_update();
    bool f = NiAdditionalGeometryData::GetShadowSceneNodeForIndex(0)->FUN_00870770();
>>>
